<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Compromise of Caspe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1412">1412</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Compromise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspe">Caspe</a> was the agreement of 1412 by which nine delegates from Aragon, Catalonia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, meeting at Caspe, chose a new king after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-of-aragon">Martin the Humane</a> died without a legitimate heir in 1410. They selected the Castilian prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-aragon">Ferdinand of Antequera</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-urgell">James II of Urgell</a> and other claimants, bringing the Trastámara dynasty to the Crown of Aragon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/compromise-of-caspe.jpg" alt="Compromise of Caspe" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raimundo Batlle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acta_original_del_Compromiso_de_Caspe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
